{#
    FRAGMENT, not a document. This file is concatenated into the sales
    channel's mail header/footer by
    `MailService::buildContents()`:

        sprintf('%s%s%s', $headerHtml, $data['contentHtml'], $footerHtml)

    The header comes from `mail_header_footer_translation.header_html`, and it
    is a *closed* 760px table: it opens a card, puts the logo in it and closes
    it again. Anything this template emits therefore lands after that card, not
    inside it.

    That is why a full `<!DOCTYPE html><html><body>` document here is wrong on
    two counts: the doctype ends up in the middle of the mail, and the body
    renders as a second, narrower white block underneath the logo — which is
    exactly the reported "logo part is wider than the white background below
    it". Shopware's own mail templates are fragments for the same reason; see
    vendor/shopware/core/Migration/Fixtures/mails/*/de-html.html.twig.

    The 760px/40px below are not arbitrary: they mirror the configured header
    card so that the logo block and this block read as one continuous white
    card. If the shop ever changes headerHtml, re-check both numbers here.

    The subject is NOT a <title> — the mailer passes it separately as
    `$data['subject']`, resolved in ReviewReminderMailer::resolveSubject().

    Copy arrives as pre-resolved `labels` from
    ReviewReminderTranslationService. Do not reintroduce `|trans` here: in 6.7
    it resolves only from the `snippet` table, which never contains this
    plugin's keys, and it renders the literal key into the mail.

    @sw-package framework
#}
{#
    The outer wrapper carries the same grey as the configured header wrapper
    (`background:#f5f5f5`). Without a <body> the canvas behind this block
    defaults to white, so a white card on white loses its edge and the two
    cards stop reading as one. bgcolor is added alongside the CSS because
    Outlook ignores background-color on tables. The 40px padding of the inner
    card matches the header's `padding:30px 40px 10px 40px`, so logo and
    content line up on the same left edge.
#}
<table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" bgcolor="#f5f5f5" style="background:#f5f5f5;" lang="{{ languageLocale|default('en-GB') }}">
    <tr>
        <td align="center">

            <table width="760" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="background:#ffffff;">
                <tr>
                    <td style="padding:24px 40px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;">

                        <h1 style="font-size:20px;margin:0 0 16px;">
                            {{ labels.reviewReminderHeadline|default('')|sw_sanitize }}
                        </h1>

                        <p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;margin:0 0 24px;">
                            {{ labels.reviewReminderIntro|default('')|sw_sanitize }}
                        </p>

                        <ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0;">
                            {% for product in products %}
                                <li style="margin-bottom:16px;border-bottom:1px solid #eeeeee;padding-bottom:12px;">
                                    {% if product.coverMediaUrl %}
                                        <img src="{{ product.coverMediaUrl }}" alt="" width="80"
                                             style="float:left;display:block;width:80px;height:auto;margin:0 12px 4px 0;border-radius:3px;" />
                                    {% endif %}
                                    <strong style="font-size:15px;">{{ product.name|sw_sanitize }}</strong>

                                    <div style="clear:both;"></div>

                                    <p style="margin:12px 0 0;">
                                        <a href="{{ product.reviewUrl }}"
                                           style="display:inline-block;background:#000000;color:#ffffff;padding:10px 16px;text-decoration:none;border-radius:3px;font-size:14px;">
                                            {{ labels.reviewReminderCta|default('')|sw_sanitize }}
                                        </a>
                                    </p>
                                </li>
                            {% endfor %}
                        </ul>

                        <p style="font-size:12px;color:#888888;margin:24px 0 0;">
                            {{ labels.reviewReminderFooter|default('')|sw_sanitize }}
                        </p>

                    </td>
                </tr>
            </table>

        </td>
    </tr>
</table>
